258:-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
259:-- 2. Room access rules (ConversationResolverService.assertRoomAccess).
260:-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
261:-- Pure function of the two rows; null = allowed, otherwise the reason.
262:-- Mirrors the TypeScript rule: different (non-null) companies deny; with an
263:-- access_control object, a non-empty allowedUsers must contain users.id, a
264:-- non-empty allowedRoles must contain the user's role, and a room that is not
265:-- public (JavaScript truthiness of isPublic) with no allowed users/roles
266:-- denies a user without a company; a falsy access_control (null, false, 0,
267:-- "") skips the access-control checks, as in TypeScript. A malformed
268:-- allowedUsers/allowedRoles (neither an array nor null) denies (stricter than
269:-- the TypeScript rule, which would treat a string by its characters).
270:create or replace function private.room_access_denial(p_user public.users, p_space public.spaces)
271:returns text
272:language plpgsql
273:stable
274:set search_path = ''
275:as $$
276:declare
